stice  Don McGann got subpoenaed  he is still also a lawyer with the Jones  day law firm so it would be interesting  to know what Jones Day has to say about  one of their own lawyers disregarding a  subpoena thinking that they are above  the law you can't ignore a subpoena  folks I mean let's get that out of the  way right now if you get subpoenaed you  are legally obligated to show up and the  House of Representatives does have a  mechanism to force this they subpoenaed  McGann he said I'm not showing up they  can send the sergeant-at-arms to go and  arrest him throw him in the little bitty  jail that they have right there at the  House of Representatives until he agrees  to testify they have the authority and  the power to do that but they're not  going to and that's the most  disappointing thing out of all of this  is that they're not going to they're  just gonna set up yet another legal  battle against the president the  Democrats are likely going to win just  like they're winning the other ones but  times a factor right okay they've got  what 18 months 18 months before the  election and if they lose their majority  in that election it's not likely but it  is possible obviously  then suddenly any talk of impeachment is  out the window it will never happen at  that point so rather than having to send  this to court get the courts to enforce  it they'll side with the Democrats then  the president appeals and appeals until  he gets all the way to the Supreme Court  that could take more than 18 months and  I know based on some of the other cases  that we have already seen the judges  typically do expedite these but we can't  guarantee something like that would  happen every single time especially when  you have a White House filing a lawsuit  or Democrats filing a lawsuit at every  possible opportunity use the mechanisms  you have in place throw McGann in your  tiny little Jail and wait for him to  start singing because McGann's made it  clear he actually did want to testify  but he's kind of between a rock and a  hard  place he thinks that it's best to listen  to the president rather than listening  to Congress he seems to forget that at  the end of the day Congress has just as  much if not more in this particular  situation power then the President does  and they can make his life hell if they  choose to do so and I think at this  point it's time for them to choose to do  so not just because of McGann's  testimony either but to send a message  it's time to tell this White House that  you are not above the law that your  administration officials are not above  the law and that when this branch of the  government that has the responsibility  of oversight of the executive branch  comes calling you have to pick up the  phone you don't have a choice  unfortunately leadership in the House of  Representatives right now is at least  giving the appearance of being  exceptionally weak not saying they are  exactly weak but by not impeaching  they're coming across as weak they may  have some kind of grand strategy that we  don't know about they may be playing a  longer game they may have an ace up  their sleeves that we don't even know  exists but by not knowing those things  it makes them look weak it makes them  look like they're afraid I mean we've  heard them say that oh the public  doesn't support impeachment who cares  the public didn't support bailing out  the big banks but you did that anyway  the public didn't support the Republican  tax scam but they did that anyway the  public didn't support the Republicans  health care plan two years ago but they  tried to do that anyway since when does  public opinion actually weigh on the  minds of members of Congress you guys  every day do stuff that the public says  that's a bad idea we want this instead  you never listen to them and then on  this one issue where you shouldn't  listen to them you're using the public  as an excuse to not go forward with it  just do it just do it that's it  there's no questioning this there's no  being mealy-mouthed there's no being  wishy-washy this needs to happen not  just to get McGann's testimony but to  restore some sense of order and  accountability to Congress one of  today's sponsors is impeach the card  slap game you can't slap Donald Trump in  real life but you can slap them in this  hilarious fast-paced two-player card  game and you can get it for ten percent  off when you go to david pakman.com  slash impeach impeach the card game is  awesome for parties or when you're  having a few drinks I've been playing it  with some friends of mine it combines  clever satire about the Trump  administration with really funny  high-quality cartoon artwork all in a  very lively card game that's easy to  learn but it stays interesting every  time you play it because of how well  designed it is and how much thought went  into the humor and the political  commentary impeach the cards slap game  is perfect if you're looking for  something fun and casual to do with your  politically minded friends or family  members it'll make a perfect gift for  anyone you know who has a sense of humor  about Donald Trump don't forget that  Father's Day is coming up and when you  go to david pakman.com slash impeach not  only will you get 10% off the game you  can also get 10% off all of the other  hilarious clothing and accessories in  their online store t-shirts coffee mugs  tote bags featuring funny political  cartoons about trump that you can't find  anywhere else get a super fun witty gift  for yourself or someone you know whether  it's impeach the card slap game or  anything else in the gift shop and get  10% off all of it when you go to david  pakman.com slash impeach

